{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": [
      "dom",
      "dom.iterable",
      "esnext"
    ],
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "incremental": true,
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ],
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./*"
      ],
      "@shared/*": [
        "../shared/*"
      ]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    "../shared/**/*.ts",
    "../shared/**/*.tsx",
    // shared/web/ is the BROWSER half of shared/ — the seams both front doors
    // render (FormShell, formatCount, the cache store, the draft hook). It is
    // .tsx as well as .ts, and it is excluded from every worker's tsconfig,
    // which has no DOM.
    // THE KIT'S COMPOSITIONS ARE IN THIS PROGRAM, and until 2026-08-28 they
    // were excluded. The exclusion's reason — "a .png import is a string
    // [under vite]; under Next it is a StaticImageData" — stopped being true
    // at kit v1.2.3, which reads every asset import through
    // shared/ui/lib/asset-url.ts. Both of its other clauses were already
    // false: "neither door imports them" (web/components/record-chrome.tsx
    // imports templates/record-chrome), and "the kit's own `npm run check`
    // typechecks them upstream" — upstream checks them under VITE, which is
    // the one toolchain that cannot see a Next-only fault.
    //
    // Measured before removing it: an exclusion does not un-check an IMPORTED
    // file (tsc pulls it in through the import graph), so it only ever hid the
    // 46 compositions nothing imports yet — exactly the ones the app is about
    // to start using. A deliberate type error in templates/rail.tsx left
    // `npm run check` green with the exclusion and turns it red without.
    //
    // THE COST, stated rather than discovered: a composition this app does not
    // use can now turn the build red on a sync. That is the trade being made
    // on purpose — a kit screen that does not compile under Next is something
    // to learn at the sync, not on the day somebody first imports it.
    ".next-avatar-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-borderfix-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-breadcrumbs-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-empty-collection-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-hoverfill-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-list-mark-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-member-row-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-nested-toolbars-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-rail-fixes-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-rail-regression-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-rail-toggle-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-tabs-underline-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-toolbar-shape-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-verify-toolbars/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next-verify/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts",
    "next-env.d.ts",
    ".next-filters-sort-verify/types/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "e2e/**",
    "playwright.config.ts"
  ]
}
